.Dd March 2026
.Dt UNJBT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm unjbt
.Nd list, test, or extract.jbt/.orb/.rbb archives
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl V
.Nm
.Op Fl l | Fl Z
.Op Fl C | Fl LL | Fl W
.Op Fl q | Fl qq | Fl v
.Op Fl x Ar pattern ...
.Op Fl i Ar pattern ...
.Ar archive
.Nm
.Op Fl K Ar key | Fl -key Ar key | Fl -key-file Ar path
.Op Fl -iv Ar iv | Fl -iv-file Ar path
.Op Fl t | Fl f | Fl u | Fl n | Fl j
.Op Fl C | Fl LL | Fl W
.Op Fl q | Fl qq | Fl v
.Op Fl d Ar dir | Fl -extract-to Ar dir
.Op Fl x Ar pattern ...
.Op Fl i Ar pattern ...
.Ar archive
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
operates on ZIP-based archives
.Pq .jbt , .rb , or .orb
whose entries may be encrypted with BFCodec (Blowfish-derived, CBC).
By default it extracts all entries into the current directory
.Pq or Fl d Ns / Ns Fl -extract-to Ar dir
and decrypts each extracted file in place.
.Pp
Listing
.Pq Fl l , Fl Z
and version
.Pq Fl V
do not require a key or IV.
Extraction, test
.Pq Fl t ,
and stdout modes
.Pq Fl c , Fl p
require key and IV unless only listing.
Key and IV can be given as hex strings
.Pq Fl K Ns / Ns Fl -key , Fl -iv ;
spaces in hex are ignored.
Alternatively use binary files:
.Fl -key-file
.Pq first 16 bytes used; file may be longer ,
.Fl -iv-file
.Pq first 8 bytes used; file may be longer .
The IV in hex is 16 hex digits (8 bytes).
If
.Fl -iv
and
.Fl -iv-file
are omitted, a default IV is used.
.Pp
Include/exclude and optional
.Ar file
arguments filter which members are listed or extracted.
Patterns are shell-style globs;
.Fn fnmatch
rules apply.
Excludes are applied first; if any include patterns are given, an entry must match at least one include and no exclude.
.Pp
If libplist is available, binary plist files are converted to XML after decryption.
PNG images containing the CgBI chunk (e.g. from iOS) can be repaired using
.Xr pngdefry 1
or, on macOS,
.Nm xcrun
.Nm pngcrush
when available.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-x pattern"
.It Fl V
Print version and exit.
.It Fl l
List archive contents in short format (length, date, time, name).
Does not require key/IV.
.It Fl Z
List archive contents in zipinfo-style format (permissions, size, date, name).
Does not require key/IV.
.It Fl t
Test archive: extract to a temporary directory, decrypt, then remove.
Reports whether the archive is intact.
.It Fl c
Extract to stdout with member names.
Not yet implemented.
.It Fl p
Extract to stdout (data only).
Not yet implemented.
.It Fl f
Freshen: extract only files that are newer than existing files on disk.
.It Fl u
Update: like freshen, and also extract files that do not exist on disk.
.It Fl n
Never overwrite existing files.
.It Fl j
Junk paths: do not recreate directory structure; extract all files into the extraction directory.
.It Fl q
Quiet: reduce messages.
.It Fl qq
Very quiet: minimal output.
.It Fl v
Verbose.
.It Fl C
Case-insensitive matching for include/exclude patterns and optional file list.
.It Fl LL
Convert extracted member names to lowercase.
.It Fl W
With pattern matching, treat
.Sq *
and
.Sq ?
as not matching
.Sq / .
.It Fl d Ar dir , Fl -extract-to Ar dir
Extraction directory.
Default is the current directory
.Pq \&. .
.It Fl x Ar pattern , Fl -exclude Ar pattern
Exclude members matching
.Ar pattern .
May be repeated.
Excludes are applied before includes.
.It Fl i Ar pattern , Fl -include Ar pattern
Include only members matching
.Ar pattern .
May be repeated.
If no include patterns are given, all non-excluded members are included.
.El
.Sh Key and IV options
.Bl -tag -width "-key-file path"
.It Fl K , Fl -key Ar key
Passphrase as hex; MD5-hashed to 16 bytes for the key.
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -key-file .
.It Fl -key-file Ar path
Read the key from the binary file
.Ar path
(first 16 bytes used; file may be longer).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -key .
.It Fl -iv Ar iv
IV as 16 hex digits (8 bytes); spaces ignored.
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -iv-file .
Default used if neither
.Fl -iv
nor
.Fl -iv-file
is given.
.It Fl -iv-file Ar path
Read the IV from the binary file
.Ar path
(first 8 bytes used; file may be longer).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -iv .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jbt 1 ,
.Xr pngdefry 1
